ful.\n\nThey might also be concerned about the cost of hiring a lawyer. So, suggesting cost-effective steps, like sending a formal letter, could be a good alternative. It’s a balance between being proactive and resourceful without spending too much money.\n\nIn the rewrite, it’s set within \"Better Call Saul,\" so adding a character-driven approach might make it more relatable. Saul’s style is no-nonsense and detail-oriented, so advising the user to approach the situation with evidence and a clear, professional tone makes sense.\n\nI should also think about the structure—maybe starting with gathering evidence,"
